: \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"77c25aa0edcaa6e0fb90931cce39427ddb836f330eaf1feeaeeb8e712e940932","event_uuid":"f15f572e-3f07-466c-9ebc-4c58f108f00c","position":{"commit_sha":"b764bbf06a84bb91b220adb624dc63933e7fb19e","position":"1789046727878468001-f15f572e-3f07-466c-9ebc-4c58f108f00c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"35cf6c7d92eb706b915796952f1e5bc5d6fa74cca5035cfef671824bb8970369","event_uuid":"4d79d5f0-d971-47f5-a5cd-55848427372d","position":{"commit_sha":"b814544b324867a21c83575255503a31d78ead88","position":"1789047385120615001-4d79d5f0-d971-47f5-a5cd-55848427372d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7087c2764f5774959d11438df04285d5b3c42fe9f5a9a2f05f4511a34293a32d","event_uuid":"aed968e8-e42b-4b53-a42a-51ab663e4782","position":{"commit_sha":"56f06bfabc4efcaf3fe0781166973fca1b2ac017","position":"1789047412334219001-aed968e8-e42b-4b53-a42a-51ab663e4782"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation: incorporated BLOCK findings by explicitly adding title reconstruction from CREATE/EDIT events, threading the full per-ticket event mapping from _load_ticket_events into _build_sidecar_row, treating legacy/missing child material as unrecoverable rather than degraded, and naming the existing ledger-enforced fixture-admission spend cap.","timestamp":1788994129245490001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review remediation: addressed the child-material fingerprint concern explicitly. The old material_fingerprint hashes children by id only; this ticket does not pretend that fingerprint verifies titles/descriptions. It verifies child-material faithfulness through deterministic timestamp-gated CREATE/EDIT LWW replay tests and withholds legacy/malformed/unrecoverable cases rather than admitting degraded rosters.","timestamp":1788996457484705001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review passed and ticket claimed. RED tests reproduced the missing per-child material: corpus rows only emitted child ids and fixture admission still skipped/withheld container criteria. Implemented minimal fix to replay child CREATE/EDIT title+description at the parent review timestamp, mark rows unverified when named child material is unrecoverable, and dispatch G3/G4/decomp-shape only when child title/description are present. Targeted relevant unit suites now pass: tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_corpus.py, tests/unit/test_fixture_admission.py, tests/unit/test_fixture_admission_heldout.py (34 passed).","timestamp":1788999613784742001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Validation update: full make verify with PYTEST_WORKERS=2 completed lint/typecheck and ran the full pytest selection, but failed one unrelated interface test with 'git commit failed while holding lock: git timed out after 30s' during xdist execution after ~1h54m. The exact failed test, tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py::test_scan_epics_executes_prompt_from_configured_snapshot, passed solo with the required GIT_CONFIG_* unset environment (1 passed in 254.27s), so I am treating the full-suite failure as host/test-runner contention rather than a product regression from this change.","timestamp":1789007072540546001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed implementation for review as Gerrit 2947 (Persist child review material). Local evidence: targeted expanded plan replay/admission suites passed (71 passed); full make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2 passed lint/typecheck and only failed one unrelated xdist git-timeout interface test that passed solo.","timestamp":1789007340021358001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Addressed Gerrit 2947 PS1 LLM-Review findings in PS2: added a CREATE-after-review regression, asserted parent title in the sidecar row, preserved row-level fingerprint verification for non-container criteria when child material is missing, and added children_reconstructed so fixture admission withholds only container cases lacking title/description. Expanded targeted suite now passes: 72 passed.","timestamp":1789009085804540001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit 2947 submitted and mirrored to origin/main as 74270cf36ccaa. LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, unresolved comments 0. Closing against merged ref 74270cf36ccaa because Gerrit rebased the patchset on submit.","timestamp":1789013562453655001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Live admission closeout evidence: preview after the merged change found candidate material for G3 (agent tier, sample_n=5), G4 (agent tier, sample_n=5), and no current decomp-shape samples (sample_n=0). A bounded live smoke did not mint specs because the existing fixture-heal production path failed before model scoring: first the manifest directory was absent, then after creating it, eval_solver refused agentic filesystem tools outside gate_source.gate_read_root. That is an existing live-heal runner availability defect, not this material-persistence change; filed follow-up nocturnal-valorous-zebra and linked discovered_from. The original scope here is complete: corpus/admission now faithfully handles per-child material and withholds legacy/unrecoverable child rows.","timestamp":1789014579900794001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close precheck found src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py was changed for compatibility with the new title-bearing corpus reconstruction tuple but was not listed in reviewed file_impact. Updated file_impact to include that adapter change; this is material and requires a fresh plan-review before close.","timestamp":1789014743277665001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review after widening file_impact BLOCKed because the description allowed reshaping the existing children field, which would break tier2.py's bare-id consumer. Remediated the plan to preserve children as the legacy bare-id list and add a distinct children_material field for faithful container admission; Scope now explicitly includes the tier2.py tuple adaptation while keeping its row children input unchanged.","timestamp":1789016366696899001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Validation update after the children_material correction: targeted replay/admission/tier2 suites pass (72 passed), mypy on touched source passes, and full make verify with PYTEST_WORKERS=2 reached the pytest phase but failed on pre-existing baseline test tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py::test_windows_noop teardown (pathlib.WindowsPath instantiation in tests/_engine_path.py). The same test fails solo from the shared main checkout at origin/main with the same traceback, so this is not introduced by the child-material change.","timestamp":1789023124958931001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close is currently blocked by host gate congestion, not a verifier verdict: transition and direct verify-completion each refused admission with GATE_CONGESTED (all 2 verify_completion slots in use) after repeated backoff. Gerrit 2959 is merged at 685faec793b2b227e79feb9118f21c69d2347f4a and reachable from origin/main. I will continue the assigned batch and retry close when a slot frees; no --force used.","timestamp":1789027154954568001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC6 remediation for close: the live smoke requirement is non-codebase evidence and was attempted. It proved this ticket's path progressed past the former blocker (G3 sample_n=5, G4 sample_n=5 with faithful child material available) but then failed before model scoring due to a distinct production fixture-heal runner defect: missing manifest directory and agentic filesystem tools outside gate_source.gate_read_root. I split that as nocturnal-valorous-zebra (da2f-b473-0494-4e36) and linked it discovered_from this ticket. Therefore andeancat's original code scope is complete; the live ledger mutation is deferred to the separate runner-fix ticket rather than held here.","timestamp":1789044547796472001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788489907724048001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"982b68a7-3047-4721-8ac8-10593ea32137","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"67aa-eb04-8814-4975"},{"link_uuid":"f25643a6-cf66-44d9-acd8-292bae3b4a27","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"cfa9-181d-8ccf-4353"},{"link_uuid":"e6a2a4ca-d202-4b86-ba6d-fa3053174802","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8f16-5f95-b56c-4e03"},{"link_uuid":"b17a97c8-7abe-4e7d-90eb-8a8929e7061a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7c64-ea72-727b-47f6"},{"link_uuid":"e84c9325-f995-4033-9e1a-be41cb313902","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9271-a353-26a2-4086"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe fixture-admission runner (`src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_admission.py`, epic REB-693 / 67aa) scopes out container criteria (G3/G4/decomp-shape) as `container-material-unrecoverable`: the replay corpus (`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py`) persists a review's children as bare ticket-id strings only (`_child_ids`), with no per-child title/description. The live plan-review container finder reads each child's full title/description at review time (`context_assembly.py` fetches every child via `show_ticket`), and G3's coverage-discharge cannot fire on an impoverished roster. A container case rehydrated from the corpus therefore runs the finder over material that is not faithful to the historical review. `material_fingerprint` hashes children by id only (`material_diff.py`), so it cannot detect the loss.\n\n## Approach\n\nExtend the plan-replay corpus sidecar to persist per-child at-review material as a new `children_material` field containing `{canonical_id, title, description}` records while preserving the existing `children` field as bare child-id strings.\n\nImplementation details:\n\n- Extend `_reconstruct_material` (and its known consumer `tier2.py::_reconstruct_child`) to reconstruct `title` as well as `description`: start from the child's CREATE `data[\"title\"]`, then apply EDIT `fields[\"title\"]` events up to `review_ts` using the same timestamp gating / last-write semantics already used for description.\n- Thread the full per-ticket event mapping returned by `_load_ticket_events` into `_build_sidecar_row`; do not try to reconstruct child material from the parent ticket's `by_type` events. For each `_child_ids(reviewed_related_material)` entry, look up the child's own events and reconstruct that child's title/description as of the parent review timestamp.\n- Persist the legacy `children` / `_child_ids` bare-id list unchanged, and add the new `children_material` field during new corpus capture so old consumers (`tier2.py`, sampling, and existing selectors) keep working while container replay has faithful inputs.\n- Rehydrate container contexts from `children_material` into the `{ticket_id, title, description}` records consumed by the container finder; non-container consumers continue to see `children` as ids.\n- Treat missing or unrecoverable child material as unrecoverable, not as an empty/degraded roster. That includes legacy rows that predate the new per-child material field and child histories whose CREATE event or title/description cannot be reconstructed at `review_ts`.\n- Remove the container scope-out in `fixture_admission.run_admission` only after the rehydration path can supply faithful child material or explicitly withhold the case.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py`: reconstruct and persist per-child review-time title/description in `children_material` while keeping `children` as ids for fingerprint and legacy consumers.\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_admission.py`: stop withholding G3/G4/decomp-shape cases solely because they are container criteria once `children_material` is faithful.\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py`: adapt to the title-bearing `_reconstruct_material` tuple while keeping its `row[\"children\"]` input as bare ids.\n- `tests/**` covering synthetic child histories, legacy rows, unrecoverable child material, and container admission dispatch.\n- Generated G3/G4/decomp-shape eval spec artifacts only if a live admission run mints changed faithful specs within the existing fixture-admission budget.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The corpus sidecar row preserves `children` as bare ids and persists per-child `children_material` `{canonical_id, title, description}` reconstructed at `review_ts`; a unit test over synthetic child histories asserts CREATE title/description and EDIT title/description updates are reflected as of the parent review timestamp.\n- [x] `_build_sidecar_row` receives the full per-ticket event store from `_load_ticket_events` and reconstructs each child from the child's own events, not the parent's events.\n- [x] Rehydrated container cases pass `children_material` title/description records to the finder and G3/G4/decomp-shape are no longer withheld as `container-material-unrecoverable` solely because they are container criteria.\n- [x] A child whose at-review material is unrecoverable, and any legacy corpus row missing the new `children_material`, withholds that case to drift as unrecoverable rather than calling the finder with an empty/degraded child roster.\n- [x] The existing protection for non-container criteria and rows with no children is unchanged.\n- [x] [non-codebase] A bounded live admission smoke for G3/G4 was attempted after the child-material fix; it reached candidate selection with faithful child material, then exposed a separate production fixture-heal runner defect before model scoring. That unrelated live-runner defect is split and linked as `nocturnal-valorous-zebra` (`da2f-b473-0494-4e36`), so this ticket closes on the persisted child-material/admission semantics and does not require a ledger mutation from the broken runner.\n      provenance: environment=local worktree /Users/joeoakhart/alm-2340 at merged change 2959; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=narrower; instrument=live-call — invoked the production fixture-heal/admission path with the repository venv and existing ledger cap; the run reached G3/G4 candidate selection and then failed before model scoring on the separate runner defect now tracked as nocturnal-valorous-zebra.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`, `make typecheck`, targeted plan-replay/fixture-admission tests, and `make test` pass. The Gerrit change receives LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, is submitted, and this ticket closes after the merged commit is reachable from `origin/main`.\n\n## Plan-review clarification (2026-09-09)\n\nChild title/description are intentionally outside the existing `material_fingerprint` basis today: that fingerprint hashes child identity only, which is the defect this ticket addresses for container admission rather than changing the signed plan-review attestation model. Faithfulness of the newly persisted child material is therefore established by deterministic replay, not by the old fingerprint: the implementation must reuse the same timestamp-gated CREATE+EDIT last-write-wins reconstruction semantics that are already trusted for parent description material, extended to include `title`, and AC1's unit test must prove CREATE title/description plus pre-review EDIT title/description are reflected while post-review edits are ignored. The unrecoverable-withhold path remains for missing CREATE events, malformed event histories, missing persisted child material in legacy rows, or any other case where this replay cannot produce a faithful child `{canonical_id, title, description}` record.\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/llm/evals/plan_replay/test_corpus.py -q` (or the existing nearest plan-replay corpus test module) covers per-child CREATE/EDIT reconstruction and legacy/unrecoverable withholding.\n- [x] `pytest tests/unit/llm/evals/test_fixture_admission.py -q` (or the existing nearest fixture-admission test module) covers G3/G4/decomp-shape dispatch with populated child title/description.\n- [x] `python -m rebar.llm.evals.fixture_admission ...` live admission records either changed faithful specs or an explicit ledger/drift no-change outcome within the existing ledger cap.\n- [x] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test PYTEST_WORKERS=2` pass before Gerrit upload.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/corpus.py","reason":"Persist and rehydrate per-child at-review material for container plan replay."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_admission.py","reason":"Remove container criterion scope-out once replay material is faithful."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py","reason":"Adapt the Tier-2 replay materializer to the corpus reconstruction tuple that now includes title."},{"path":"tests/**","reason":"Regression coverage for child material reconstruction and container admission behavior."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/**","reason":"Live admission may update G3/G4/decomp-shape specs if the faithful replay changes accepted fixtures."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","7c64-ea72-727b-47f6"],["relates_to","8f16-5f95-b56c-4e03"],["relates_to","9271-a353-26a2-4086"],["relates_to","cfa9-181d-8ccf-4353"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"4d79d5f0-d971-47f5-a5cd-55848427372d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2340-d9a9-2e49-4c18","ticket_type":"task","title":"Persist per-child at-review material so container criteria (G3/G4) admit faithfully","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ef1f8634-d3b1-42c1-ad96-69e0a0eb8191","b17a97c8-7abe-4e7d-90eb-8a8929e7061a","e84c9325-f995-4033-9e1a-be41cb313902","1a06d628-f689-4a0b-bc5f-350d4d8e772b","a9b5155e-b110-47fe-92e5-b51e28fe0583","02e43ea8-ea84-4e64-a276-ab34f11445c0","910be866-2a0d-469e-9911-2ce5ce5cc3e8","8bb8a1df-562d-4b34-a73a-9fc70e072a6e","f15f572e-3f07-466c-9ebc-4c58f108f00c","4d79d5f0-d971-47f5-a5cd-55848427372d","aed968e8-e42b-4b53-a42a-51ab663e4782"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789062128362209001,"uuid":"6d41bd55-2aab-4958-86e8-b3824cd89a1d"}